  "query_preview": "period. Trends have shifted more towards a solution that\nhas the boundary eventually washing out as the low weakens, \nleaving behind a plume of moisture across the Florida peninsula. \nThe high to the north of Florida looks to gradually shift eastward\nand eventually offshore, with another surface high from the Great\nLakes region shifting eastward to replace it. Overall, little \nchange is anticipated relative to the broad pattern across east \ncentral Florida, with persistent breezy northeast flow maintaining\nhazardous beach and boating conditions. Onshore-moving showers \nare forecast to persist mid to late week, with the highest rain \nchances remaining focused along the coast. A low chance for storm \ndevelopment will also continue across the local waters and \nprimarily along the coast. Temperatures are forecast to remain \nseasonable and near-normal values for this time of year.",
